# 2026-10-09 (Q4 review, overdue from Q3; VV): every entry removed. The
# trivy-reconcile diagnostic of that day (run 37937876962) scanned all five
# published `:latest` images at every severity, with unfixed findings shown and
# WITHOUT this file applied, and found 0 vulnerabilities on each of backend, db,
# frontend, mcp-server and nginx. So no listed id matched anything any more:
#   - Build-stage-only (`alpine/git`, `node:24-alpine`, 32 ids): never scannable.
#     All three Trivy jobs run `trivy image` against published runtime
#     manifests, and a build stage is never in one. Do not list build-stage
#     CVEs here; they cannot reach a deployed instance or the gate.
#   - `gosu` in `postgres:18-alpine` (28 ids): upstream rebuilt it on a patched
#     Go toolchain. An unfixed upstream-binary CVE cannot fail the gate anyway
#     (`ignore-unfixed: true`), so such an entry only hides it from the daily
#     observe scan, which is the one scan meant to show it.
#   - `nghttp2` (CVE-2026-27135) and pip's vendored setuptools/msgpack
#     (CVE-2025-47273, CVE-2026-59890, GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964): the transitional
#     entries whose own comments said to drop them once a rebuilt image scanned
#     clean. The runtime images ship no pip since 2026-07-30.
#
# Prove an entry absent with trivy-reconcile.yml (default `upload_sarif=false`),
# never with the daily scan: the daily scan applies this file, so it cannot see
# what the file hides.
#
# This file is intentionally empty of entries until a finding needs one.
